"payments\",\n              \"shipping\",\n              \"returns\"\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"order_id\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: What's happening with my order ORD-716247?\n\nReply with only a JSON array of the tool calls that fulfil the request, each of the form {\"name\": \"<tool name>\", \"arguments\": {...}}, where \"arguments\" is a JSON object (not a string). When the request needs several calls, list them all. Reply with [] if no tool fits the request, or if the request does not give a value for a required argument: never guess one. Include every required argument. Include an optional argument only if the request asks for a value for it; otherwise leave it out and the tool applies its default. Give each value the type its schema declares: JSON numbers for integer and number, true or false for boolean, and strings for string, copied exactly as written.","role":"user"},{"content":"[{\"name\":\"get_order_status\",\"arguments\":{\"order_id\":\"ORD-716247\"}}]","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool results:\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"get_order_status\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"order_id\": \"ORD-716247\",\n      \"status\": \"shipped\",\n      \"carrier\": \"usps\",\n      \"tracking_number\": \"71141662778\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: Where is that parcel right now?\n\nReply as before: only a JSON array of tool calls, or [] if no tool fits or a required value is missing.","role":"user"}]